  - title: Go or stay
    number: 8
    heartsNeeded: 8
    path: 0
    conditions:
      days: 0
      seasons: 0
      dayFrom: 0
      dayTo: 0
      minYear: 0
      minTotalDays: 0
      weather: 0
      requireFlags: []
      anyFlags: []
      forbidFlags: []
      counters: []
    pages:
    - I have to tell the course by Friday.
    - If I go, I learn how big companies work. How the tower works. Then maybe one day I come back and beat them properly.
    - If I stay, I do it now, my way. The games corner, the slush trick, everything. Small, but real.
    - Mom and Dad say it's my choice. Which is worse, honestly. What would you do?
    happy: 0
    ask:
      item: {fileID: 0}
      amount: 0
      minQuality: 0
      questTitle: 
      questText: 
      reminder: []
      thanks: []
    choice:
      enabled: 1
      optionA: Take the course
      replyA:
      - The course. Okay. Okay, wow.
      - I'm going to tell Dad tonight. If you hear shouting, it's me, from happiness. Probably.
      flagsA:
      - jiho_business_course
      optionB: Stay and change the store
      replyB:
      - Stay. Yeah. I think I knew that already. I just needed someone else to say it.
      - Right. I'm going to need a screwdriver, two arcade machines and my dad in a very good mood.
      flagsB:
      - jiho_games_corner
    setFlags: []
    reward:
      gold: 0
      item: {fileID: 0}
      amount: 0
      friendship: 0
  - title: Weekend ideas
    number: 9
    heartsNeeded: 9
    path: 1
    conditions:
      days: 0
      seasons: 0
      dayFrom: 0
      dayTo: 0
      minYear: 0
      minTotalDays: 0
      weather: 0
      requireFlags: []
      anyFlags: []
      forbidFlags: []
      counters: []
    pages:
    - First month of the course. I come home every weekend with a notebook full of ideas, and Dad pretends he isn't reading them.
    - Do you know the tower loses money on half of what it sells? On purpose. To kill small shops. Then it puts the prices back up. There's a name for it in the textbook.
    - I'm going to find every trick they use, and then I'm going to find the trick that beats it.
    happy: 0
    ask:
      item: {fileID: 0}
      amount: 0
      minQuality: 0
      questTitle: 
      questText: 
      reminder: []
      thanks: []
